  "slug": "age-dependent-huntington-7aeb",
  "summary": "Recent preprints map cell-type-specific and temporal molecular changes in neurons, including TDP-43 interactome shifts and lysosome trafficking control.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how neurons maintain organelle and proteome integrity under cell-type- or stage-specific perturbation. Fmr1-KO profiling reports cell type-specific mRNA and protein remodelling at cortical excitatory and inhibitory synapses, and SETX knockout in human iPSC-derived motor neurons impairs neurite growth, synaptic activity and survival in a stage-dependent manner. A temporal APEX2 atlas of TDP-43 interactomes shows network changes persisting beyond stress granule clearance. Lysosomal quality control is addressed in two items: the axon initial segment is proposed as a lysosome trafficking checkpoint, with MCF2L anchoring lysosomes via gAnkG, and processing bodies promote lysosomal quality and survival during recovery from lysosomal damage. Contact-phagy adds a selective autophagy route that turns over ER-mitochondria contact-site subdomains. The lysosome and contact-site studies are primarily mechanistic and not disease-specific.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
